<sys:String x:Key="Startup.Title">Startup apps</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Startup.Toggle">Enable / Disable</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Startup.Note">Sources: HKCU/HKLM ...\CurrentVersion\Run (and WOW6432Node) and both Startup folders. Enable / Disable writes the same Explorer\StartupApproved flag Windows Task Manager uses; the Run entry itself is never changed. Machine-wide (HKLM) entries need administrator rights. Packaged (Store) startup tasks are not read.</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Startup.NeedsAdmin">{0} is a machine-wide entry; changing it needs administrator rights.</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Startup.Failed">Could not change the startup entry</sys:String>

<sys:String x:Key="Services.Title">Services</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Services.Note">Source: OpenSCManagerW + EnumServicesStatusExW. Refreshed on the 4-second slow tier.</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Apps.Title">Installed apps</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Apps.Note">Source: the Uninstall registry keys (HKLM 64-bit and 32-bit, HKCU) that Settings › Apps also reads, refreshed every 30 s. System components and updates are hidden, as in Settings. Store (MSIX) apps are not listed yet.</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Drivers.Title">Drivers</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Drivers.Note">Source: Service Control Manager entries of type SERVICE_DRIVER, start type from QueryServiceConfigW, version and vendor from each .sys file's version resource. Refreshed every 60 s.</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Sources.Title">Sources</sys:String>
<sys:String x:Key="Sources.Note">The health of every data source. Each source reports its own health; one failure never blanks the others. Unavailable means this PC does not have that data source at all.</sys:String>

